.SH Basics in detail
This page adds the details to ../basics.md: the error codes, every error
value, the limits, the nesting depth, memory, threads and owners.
.SS 1. Error codes
\f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] is an error code enum:
\f[CR]std::is_error_code_enum\f[R] is true for it.
A \f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] converts to a \f[CR]std::error_code\f[R] with
the category \f[CR]cbor\f[R].
\f[CR]message()\f[R] gives the text of the error.
.IP
.EX
std::error_code const e = cbor::error::key_not_found;
e.message();          \f[I]// \(dqkey not found\(dq\f[R]
e.category().name();  \f[I]// \(dqcbor\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Four errors compare equal to a \f[CR]std::errc\f[R].
No other error compares equal to a \f[CR]std::errc\f[R].
The comparison needs a \f[CR]std::error_code\f[R] on the left: a
\f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] and a \f[CR]std::errc\f[R] do not compare
directly, and that does not compile.
.PP
