.SS 2. Wrong use
A wrong use of the library does not compile where the compiler can see
it.
A temporary \f[CR]std::string\f[R] as the bytes of a view is one
example.
Where the compiler cannot see a wrong use, the library throws
\f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 2
an empty owner, or a null \f[CR]std::shared_ptr<std::string const>\f[R];
.IP \(bu 2
a \f[CR]cbor::lazy{}\f[R] that holds no item.
